Method Endpoint Description GET <code>/api/v1/admin/feature-flags</code> List all flags PUT <code>/api/v1/admin/feature-flags/{key}</code> Enable/disable a flag <p>Update body:</p> <pre><code>{
  "enabled": true,
  "description": "Allow checkout without an account"
}
</code></pre>

POST /api/v1/seller/pos/sales <pre><code>{
  "items": [
    { "productId": "product-uuid", "quantity": 2 }
  ],
  "warehouseId": "warehouse-uuid",
  "paymentMethod": "COD",
  "customerEmail": "walkin@example.com",
  "posSessionId": "session-uuid"
}
</code></pre> <ul> <li>Optionally validated against a POS-enabled warehouse owned by the seller.</li> <li>All items must belong to the seller’s shop.</li> <li>Items may include <code>variantId</code>; variant prices and warehouse stock are used.</li> <li>Creates a completed order with <code>fulfillmentType = POS</code>, <code>shippingMethod = POS</code> and zero shipping.</li> <li>Tax is calculated from the POS warehouse country and the normal tax rules.</li> <li><code>idempotencyKey</code> can be supplied to make retries safe.</li> <li>Stock is decremented at the selected POS warehouse.</li> <li><code>posSessionId</code> links the sale to an open cash-drawer session; <code>COD</code> is treated as cash and other   methods as card for drawer reconciliation.</li> <li>Decrements stock, increments sales counters, records a completed manual payment, grants digital   entitlements, awards loyalty points and emits the normal payment-completed event (seller payouts,   commission and notifications).</li> <li>Returns <code>201 Created</code> with the order.</li> </ul> GET /api/v1/seller/pos/sales

Method Endpoint Description GET <code>/api/v1/seller/pos/sessions</code> List drawer sessions POST <code>/api/v1/seller/pos/sessions/open</code> Open a drawer session POST <code>/api/v1/seller/pos/sessions/{id}/close</code> Count cash and close GET <code>/api/v1/seller/pos/sales/{id}/receipt</code> Printable sale receipt GET <code>/api/v1/seller/pos/sessions/{id}/report</code> Printable session/Z report <p>Open:</p> <pre><code>{
  "openingFloat": 100.00,
  "warehouseId": "warehouse-uuid",
  "notes": "Morning shift"
}
</code></pre> <p>Close:</p> <pre><code>{
  "countedCash": 121.00,
  "notes": "Counted by Alice"
}
</code></pre> <ul> <li>One open session is allowed per shop.</li> <li>Cash sales (<code>COD</code>) and card sales are accumulated separately.</li> <li>Closing records <code>expectedCash = openingFloat + cashSales</code>, <code>countedCash</code> and <code>variance</code>.</li> <li>Sessions remain available for POS history/export.</li> <li>Receipts and session reports are returned as printable HTML (<code>text/html</code>) and only for the   seller's own shop.</li> </ul>

POST /api/v1/policy-consents/consent <pre><code>{
  "policyId": "6c5078d3-f8e3-4c88-9afe-48b5423c664f"
}
</code></pre> <p>Consent rows are append-only: re-consenting creates a new row with <code>grantedAt</code>, and <code>DELETE /api/v1/policy-consents/{id}</code> sets <code>revokedAt</code> rather than deleting the audit trail.</p>

