POST /api/v1/disputes <pre><code>{
  "orderId": "order-uuid",
  "type": "ORDER_ISSUE",
  "subject": "Missing item",
  "description": "One item was missing from the parcel"
}
</code></pre> <p>Types: <code>ORDER_ISSUE</code>, <code>PAYOUT</code>, <code>REVIEW</code>, <code>OTHER</code>.</p> <ul> <li>A linked order is only accessible by its customer, its shop's seller, or an admin.</li> <li>Without an order, the caller's seller profile (if any) is attached.</li> <li><code>GET /api/v1/disputes</code> returns disputes where the caller is the customer or the seller.</li> </ul> <p>Admin lifecycle:</p> Status Allowed next <code>OPEN</code> <code>UNDER_REVIEW</code>, <code>RESOLVED</code>, <code>REJECTED</code> <code>UNDER_REVIEW</code> <code>RESOLVED</code>, <code>REJECTED</code> <code>RESOLVED</code> / <code>REJECTED</code> terminal <pre><code>{ "status": "RESOLVED", "resolution": "Replacement sent" }
</code></pre> <p>Resolution stores the admin user and timestamp.</p>

