POST /api/v1/admin/subscriptions/run-billing <ul> <li>with a stored payment method and <code>PAYMENT_PROVIDER=stripe</code> → charges the saved payment method   off-session. A successful charge extends the period, records a <code>PAID</code> invoice, resets dunning and   refreshes the entitlement. A <code>requires_action</code>/<code>processing</code> charge stays pending.</li> <li>without a payment method (or with the manual provider) → creates/keeps a <code>PENDING</code> invoice and   sets the subscription <code>PAST_DUE</code> for manual collection.</li> <li>failed charges record the attempt, failure reason and next retry, and keep the subscription   <code>PAST_DUE</code> during the 3-day grace period. After the configured attempts/grace period it becomes   <code>EXPIRED</code> and digital access is revoked.</li> </ul> <p>Returns:</p> <pre><code>{ "invoicesCreated": 1, "canceled": 0, "paid": 1, "failed": 0, "expired": 0 }
</code></pre> <p>Provider renewal webhooks (Stripe <code>payment_intent.*</code>) are matched by the <code>subscription_invoice_id</code> metadata and applied idempotently; a successful webhook also marks the invoice paid and activates the subscription.</p> <p>Confirm a renewal payment manually and reactivate:</p> POST /api/v1/admin/subscriptions/{id}/activate <pre><code>{ "paymentReference": "pay_renewal" }
</code></pre> <p>Marks the pending/failed invoice paid, advances the period, sets the subscription <code>ACTIVE</code>, resets dunning, and refreshes the digital entitlement expiry.</p>

Method Endpoint Description GET <code>/api/v1/admin/support/tickets?status=&amp;priority=&amp;assignedTo=</code> Filtered list GET <code>/api/v1/admin/support/tickets/{id}</code> Full thread incl. internal notes POST <code>/api/v1/admin/support/tickets/{id}/messages</code> Reply or internal note PUT <code>/api/v1/admin/support/tickets/{id}</code> Status/priority/category/assignment GET <code>/api/v1/admin/support/tickets/{id}/attachments/{attachmentId}</code> Admin: download a support attachment <p>Reply body:</p> <pre><code>{ "body": "Checking with the carrier", "isInternal": true }
</code></pre> <p>Update body:</p> <pre><code>{
  "status": "RESOLVED",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "category": "ORDER",
  "assignedTo": "admin-uuid"
}
</code></pre> <p>Send a blank <code>assignedTo</code> to unassign.</p> <p>Statuses: <code>OPEN</code>, <code>PENDING</code>, <code>RESOLVED</code>, <code>CLOSED</code>.</p> <p>SLA targets by priority:</p> Priority First response Resolution <code>URGENT</code> 1 hour 4 hours <code>HIGH</code> 4 hours 24 hours <code>NORMAL</code> 24 hours 72 hours <code>LOW</code> 48 hours 120 hours <p>Ticket responses include <code>firstResponseAt</code>, <code>responseDueAt</code>, <code>resolutionDueAt</code> and <code>slaBreached</code>. The first admin reply records <code>firstResponseAt</code>.</p> <ul> <li><code>RESOLVED</code> / <code>CLOSED</code> record <code>resolvedAt</code>.</li> <li><code>OPEN</code> clears <code>resolvedAt</code>.</li> <li>Every reply updates <code>lastMessageAt</code>, which drives the queue ordering.</li> </ul>
